=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-28T13:17:45Z","updated_at":"2024-10-28T13:17:45Z","body":"Because it's the wrong name, you've added the same name twice, it added the one you missed","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2441565576/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443553891","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557#issuecomment-2443553891","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98557","id":2443553891,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Rpaxj","user":{"login":"Summersay415","id":71974498,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxOTc0NDk4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71974498?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415","html_url":"https://github.com/Summersay415","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Summersay415/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T08:27:46Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T08:27:46Z","body":"> See also #98606 for another alternative\r\n\r\nPersonally I prefer this one instead of #98606.\r\nBecause, GDScript is simple language. Why you need to write \"@protected/private\" every time you declare a variable when you can just use a '_' prefix? And what you will do in moments when you forced to violate access limitation? Here, you can just ignore the warning. And in #98606 you can do... nothing. In GDScript there is no need for annotation complexity. Instead, we can just properly document this prefixes.\r\n\r\nAlso, I think '__' should be private, not protected, because private access is very strict, and I think it will be rarely used - protected is enough in most cases","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443553891/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443624403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557#issuecomment-2443624403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98557","id":2443624403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Rpr_T","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T09:00:53Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T09:35:17Z","body":"> > See also #98606 for another alternative\r\n> \r\n> Personally I prefer this one instead of #98606. Because, GDScript is simple language. Why you need to write \"@protected/private\" every time you declare a variable when you can just use a '_' prefix? And what you will do in moments when you forced to violate access limitation? Here, you can just ignore the warning. And in #98606 you can do... nothing. In GDScript there is no need for annotation complexity. Instead, we can just properly document this prefixes.\r\n> \r\n> Also, I think '__' should be private, not protected, because private access is very strict, and I think it will be rarely used - protected is enough in most cases\r\n\r\nIn one word: it not only is coherent with the philosphy of godot's implementation of new features, but also greatly simplifies the code structure and maintains the code compatibility with the one in previous godot versions at the most extend. It's both technically and executabily simple, imo.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2443624403/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2444527277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/98557#issuecomment-2444527277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98557","id":2444527277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6RtIat","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-29T15:02:36Z","updated_at":"2024-10-29T15:02:36Z","body":"Next I want to introduce `__` as private members' prefix, as someone mentioned this directly or indirectly in this post.\r\nBut whether this is needed or not still needs discussion🤔","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.gi